{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4351685","formula":"Cs₂O₂","hill":"Cs2O2","elements":["O","Cs"],"composition":{"O":2.0,"Cs":2.0},"names":{"en":"Cesium peroxide","ru":"Пероксид цезия"},"descriptions":{"en":"Caesium peroxide or cesium peroxide is an inorganic compound of caesium and oxygen with the chemical formula Cs2O2. It can be formed from caesium metal by adding a stoichiometric amount in ammonia solution, or oxidizing the solid metal directly. 2 Cs + O2 → Cs2O2 It can also be formed by the thermal decomposition of caesium superoxide: 2 CsO2 → Cs2O2 + O2 Upon heating until 650 °C, the compound will decompose to caesium monoxide and atomic oxygen: Cs2O2 → Cs2O + [O] Caesium peroxide shows a Raman vibration at 743 cm−1, due to the presence of the peroxide ions.","ru":"Перокси́д це́зия — Cs2O2, неорганическое бинарное соединение цезия с кислородом и являющееся производным пероксида водорода. Бледно-жёлтые, очень гигроскопичные, ромбические кристаллы. Сильный окислитель."},"fame":10,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-7896","atoms":20,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[4.334,0.0,0.0],[0.0,6.437,0.0],[0.0,0.0,7.558]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":1.916,"el":"Cs"},{"x":0.0,"y":6.437,"z":1.916,"el":"Cs"},{"x":4.334,"y":0.0,"z":1.916,"el":"Cs"},{"x":4.334,"y":6.437,"z":1.916,"el":"Cs"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":5.641,"el":"Cs"},{"x":0.0,"y":6.437,"z":5.641,"el":"Cs"},{"x":4.334,"y":0.0,"z":5.641,"el":"Cs"},{"x":4.334,"y":6.437,"z":5.641,"el":"Cs"},{"x":2.167,"y":0.754,"z":3.779,"el":"O"},{"x":2.167,"y":5.683,"z":3.779,"el":"O"},{"x":2.167,"y":3.219,"z":5.695,"el":"Cs"},{"x":2.167,"y":3.219,"z":1.863,"el":"Cs"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.973,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.973,"z":7.558,"el